    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "European immigrants began establishing homesteads in Batavia during the mid-1840s on fertile lands supported by tributaries of the Milwaukee River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/batavia_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Local historians regard 1851 as the year Batavia was founded, though some settlers arrived as early as 1846.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thebatavian.com/batavia-city-historian/batavia-wisconson-dont-blink-or-youll-miss-it/43540"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1900, Batavia featured a diverse array of businesses, including a carriage factory, a cigar factory, and even an egg-shaped water conduit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thebatavian.com/batavia-city-historian/batavia-wisconson-dont-blink-or-youll-miss-it/43540"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dairy farming dominated the early economy of Batavia, with local cheese factories processing milk for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/batavia_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Sheboygan County cheese producers in Batavia helped form the state's first federation of cheese factories in 1913 to stabilize market prices.",
